1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:21,000
I cannot help but be moved by the biblical truths that this little lesson contain, this track contain, and so I gratefully acknowledge whatever good there might be in this lesson I owe to Brother David Roper, and whatever bad there is in this lesson I owe to myself.

2
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:31,000
But the lesson brings into focus very sharply the limitations that we must impose upon human language, or rather that are imposed upon human language.

3
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:46,000
For if it was possible for me this morning to have a full command of the words and the moods and the shades of meaning to express vividly the ideas, and ideas are just mental images of the lesson of the truth that this lesson contain,

4
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:53,000
there isn't a single person that will leave this building this morning without being firmly dedicated to the service of God.

5
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Now I don't expect that to happen. I don't expect that everyone that is here this morning will leave this building firmly dedicated to the service of God.

6
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:11,000
But that sad fact is simply owing to the limitations that we must cope with in trying to express our thoughts.

7
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:30,000
The lesson is a narration of a story. I'm going to tell you a story. The names in the story are assumed names, but the characters may well represent someone that you know, and alas they may well represent you or they may well represent me.

8
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,000
The story is about a man, and we'll call him John.

9
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Just because John is a common name, we'll call him John Jones. The name could be your name or mine.

10
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:49,000
But we'll call him John, and the story begins on a Monday morning in the autumn months.

11
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:56,000
John is awakened early. He is awakened by a beam of sunlight, autumn sunlight.

12
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:04,000
And John feels rested and relaxed even though it's an hour earlier than his usual time for a rising to go to work.

13
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:16,000
And he thinks that since it is a beautiful, warm autumn morning, and there won't be many more days such as this before bad weather sets in, that he will walk to work.

14
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:23,000
So he gets up and dresses quietly and quickly.

15
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:28,000
And as he drinks his morning coffee, he gazes in upon the sleeping form of his wife, Mary.

16
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,720
And he smiles as he sees how comfortably she sleeps and takes her rest.

17
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:47,840
And John Jones, as he leans his hand against the post of the bedroom door, he thinks how wonderful you are, Mary, and how thankful I am that God has given me a wife like you.

18
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:54,280
Strange that John Jones should be thinking thoughts like this because John isn't a servant of God.

19
00:02:54,940 --> 00:02:56,360
John is not a Christian.

20
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:59,340
But his wife, Mary, she is a Christian.

21
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:03,860
But John has never come around yet to the point of obeying the Lord.

22
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:09,420
And as he gazes in upon her, he thinks how wonderful you are, Mary.

23
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:13,120
And I am thankful that God has given me a wife like you.

24
00:03:13,820 --> 00:03:18,520
And I know that there isn't a single phase of your life that your faith has not influenced.

25
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:21,820
And you are what you are because you are a Christian.

26
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:24,160
And I love you for that.

27
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:31,980
And as he turns from that door, he gazes in upon the sleeping form of his little boy, Billy.

28
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:41,380
And he smiles as he sees how soundly he sleeps, how he snores, and how soundly he sleeps just before the awakening hours of the morning.

29
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:48,920
And once again, this feeling of gratitude and this feeling of cry crept over John Jones that this was his little boy.

30
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:55,240
And then he turns from that door and he looks in upon the sleeping figure of his little girl, Susie.

31
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:59,080
And John Jones knew that God had been good to him.

32
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:05,020
Good to him despite the fact that John Jones had given nothing back unto God.

33
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:08,040
Funny that he should be thinking thoughts like this.

34
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:15,660
And as he walks out the door and fills his lungs with a warm autumn air, he thinks it's good to be alive.

35
00:04:15,820 --> 00:04:17,880
It is good to be alive.

36
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:20,060
And the world is quiet.

37
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:28,480
There are no sounds except the thrilling symphony of the sounds of the songs of a thousand birds that thrust forth their songs of gratitude and praise to the maker.

38
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:34,080
And John, why can't you understand?

39
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:45,660
And as he looks down the street which he lives on, he sees all the beautiful leaves on the trees, all the different shades of red and green.

40
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,800
And there's still green in the trees.

41
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:53,460
And there's all the different shades of yellow and orange and all glistening and shining in the bright autumn sun.

42
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:59,640
And John, why can't you understand that this is perhaps an omen, a message?

43
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:04,560
John, why can't you see that all of nature is dying, that it is going to sleep?

44
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:10,520
And John, why can't you see that a dying nature depicts a dying humanity?

45
00:05:11,840 --> 00:05:16,260
And John doesn't think of the fact that all of nature is going to sleep, dying.

46
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:20,400
And he does not think of the fact that he himself may die someday.

47
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:26,260
The world is quiet before the invading army of breadwinners like John.

48
00:05:27,340 --> 00:05:29,820
There are no screaming children playing in the street.

49
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:32,500
There are no housewives chattering across the back fence.

50
00:05:34,180 --> 00:05:44,260
And the air is pure from the putrefied influence of burnt gasoline that will soon be burrowed in from the army of automobiles that will be invaded in the streets and boulevards.

51
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:46,520
And it is a quiet, beautiful morning.

52
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:48,860
And John Jones is alive and he is happy.

53
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:51,440
And he is grateful to be alive.

54
00:05:52,140 --> 00:05:58,000
And as he begins his walk down the sidewalk, his thoughts go back to how good God has been to him.

55
00:05:58,380 --> 00:06:00,060
And he remembered a sermon he heard.

56
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,080
When was it?

57
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:02,840
Was it last Sunday?

58
00:06:02,940 --> 00:06:05,560
No, no, it wasn't last Sunday because that was yesterday.

59
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:11,360
And I remember when little Susie came in to ask me and to beg me to go to church.

60
00:06:11,740 --> 00:06:16,500
And I remember I told her that I was tired.

61
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:21,920
And then I realized I wasn't tired because I had slept an hour longer this morning because it was Sunday morning.

62
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:25,380
Then I told her, well, Daddy has to do some work around the house.

63
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:27,040
Susie, you go on with Mother.

64
00:06:27,580 --> 00:06:29,900
And I have to do some work around the house.

65
00:06:29,900 --> 00:06:37,580
I have to, let's see, oh, yes, I have to clean and paint the rain gutters before bad weather comes.

66
00:06:38,180 --> 00:06:43,240
And then John smiled somewhat shamefully as he remembered the excuse that he had made to his little girl.

67
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:47,620
And he remembered how Billy had wanted to stay home too because Daddy stayed home.

68
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:57,660
But he remembered he had on occasion gone to church and he had seen there seated in the pews in a row the Lemons family, the Curry family, and the Lowens family.

69
00:06:57,660 --> 00:07:06,240
And he thought how wonderful this theme that father and mother and children would all sit together, they would listen and learn together.

70
00:07:06,880 --> 00:07:19,420
And once again this feeling of John was face to face with the realization that he was letting his family down, that he was letting his God down, that he was neglecting important things.

71
00:07:19,420 --> 00:07:30,340
But he remembered he had heard a sermon two or three Sundays ago back in August when the preacher had preached on the judgment.

72
00:07:30,940 --> 00:07:38,740
And he remembered when he had read from 2 Peter and he had said that the earth and all of its works shall be burnt up.

73
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:41,140
And John didn't like to believe that.

74
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:47,160
And as he walked along, he deliberately planted his feet upon a section of sidewalk and said,

75
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:49,740
This has been here for years and years.

76
00:07:50,100 --> 00:07:51,380
It is too everlasting.

77
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:56,580
And then he walked down the street a little bit further and he came to a section of the sidewalk that was cracked.

78
00:07:56,960 --> 00:07:57,680
It was broken.

79
00:07:57,680 --> 00:08:06,300
And John said, Well, after he thought for a moment, I suppose that the most durable things that are material can fade away.

80
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:12,780
And then he continued his walk on down the sidewalk.

81
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:20,460
And as he passed the home of the Currys, he saw Mrs. Curry stick her head out the door.

82
00:08:20,460 --> 00:08:22,760
And she looked both ways.

83
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:24,900
And John stopped for a moment and smiled.

84
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:26,860
It was no doubt that she had just gotten up.

85
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:31,440
She still, her hair was a mess and she still had her robe on.

86
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:35,300
And she looked both ways up and down the street thinking that no one was looking.

87
00:08:35,420 --> 00:08:38,840
She sneaked out on the porch and got the paper and went back in the house again.

88
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:44,280
And John walked on down the sidewalk.

89
00:08:44,860 --> 00:08:47,240
It is just a world that is coming alive.

90
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:51,380
And John Jones is alive and he is grateful.

91
00:08:52,140 --> 00:08:58,360
And as he walked down the sidewalk, he could smell the odor of bacon frying across the street coming from the Ingrams' home.

92
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:03,040
And parked by the curb was a car all decorated with ribbons and crepe papers.

93
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:05,620
And placards were printed on the car.

94
00:09:05,700 --> 00:09:12,460
And he had remembered that the previous Saturday, the Ingram girl had married the Williams boy and they had flown away to California on their honeymoon.

95
00:09:12,460 --> 00:09:20,840
John, why can't you understand that in Matthew 24, that as in the days of Noah, they were marrying and giving him marriage.

96
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:23,300
And so shall it be when the Son of Man shall come.

97
00:09:23,880 --> 00:09:27,220
As in the days before the flood, they were eating and drinking.

98
00:09:27,340 --> 00:09:29,740
And so shall it be when the Son of Man shall come.

99
00:09:30,180 --> 00:09:31,300
These are warnings, John.

100
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:32,780
Why can't you understand them?

101
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:37,180
And he walks on and he hears the steady, resting tones of a man's voice speaking.

102
00:09:38,460 --> 00:09:45,380
And he realizes that this is across the street coming from a little white house that sits back off the road where old man Glazer lives.

103
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:47,620
The old fellow lives all alone.

104
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:49,160
And he is hard of hearing.

105
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:51,700
And he has his radio turned up loud in case.

106
00:09:52,260 --> 00:09:54,840
And the morning news is on.

107
00:09:54,840 --> 00:10:07,880
And he heard the commentator say that during the night that Iran and Israel and Palestine and Iraq, the leaders had gotten together and they had discussed and negotiated peace talks.

108
00:10:09,540 --> 00:10:13,120
And it seemed like once again the world was going to enjoy peace.

109
00:10:13,680 --> 00:10:18,780
John, why can't you remember a passage from Paul in 1 Thessalonians, the 5th verse.

110
00:10:18,780 --> 00:10:25,200
When they are saying peace and safety, then come a sudden destruction upon them as prevaileth upon a woman with child.

111
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:28,120
And they shall in no wise assume peace.

112
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:30,600
But John never dreamed that.

113
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:37,880
As he walks on down the street, he steps alive with youth, his raincoat over his arm in case the day should bring showers.

114
00:10:39,060 --> 00:10:42,540
John is still musing over how good it is to be alive.

115
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:47,080
And as he passes the neat trimmed houses, he is grateful for God.

116
00:10:47,180 --> 00:10:51,720
He is grateful for country and for job and for luxury and for family.

117
00:10:51,820 --> 00:10:53,660
He is grateful for so many things.

118
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:57,620
And yet the same nagging, accusing thought kept occurring to John.

119
00:10:58,100 --> 00:11:00,580
John, you have done nothing about these things.

120
00:11:01,060 --> 00:11:02,080
You have done nothing.

121
00:11:02,260 --> 00:11:07,860
And then John realized, John Jones, you're going to have to do something to show God that you're grateful for all this.

122
00:11:08,220 --> 00:11:09,660
You're going to have to obey your Lord.

123
00:11:09,660 --> 00:11:13,740
You're going to have to obey him and show him that you're grateful for all of these things.

124
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:15,700
When are you going to do it, John?

125
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:18,540
Well, I can't this Wednesday night.

126
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:20,640
That's the night that me and the fellas go bowling.

127
00:11:21,740 --> 00:11:25,480
And, well, maybe Sunday I'll go.

128
00:11:26,020 --> 00:11:34,100
And, no, no, that's the weekend that Jerry and I had planned to get one more fishing trip in before bad weather comes along.

129
00:11:34,100 --> 00:11:38,300
And one of these days, I'm going to obey the gospel.

130
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:39,660
I'm going to show God.

131
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:46,960
And then he stopped at the corner of Oak Street to let the Coca-Cola truck pass that was making his deliveries.

132
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:53,800
And John was musing over what he should do, what he was going to do, and what he intended to do someday soon.

133
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:58,120
And then he resumes his walk after the Coca-Cola truck passed.

134
00:11:58,760 --> 00:12:04,480
And John was just raising his foot to put it up on the curb when it happened.

135
00:12:05,520 --> 00:12:06,480
When it happened.

136
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:16,600
Now, John had read, and he had heard read many times in Thessalonians, the fourth chapter of 1 Thessalonians,

137
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:24,080
that the Lord himself shall descend from heaven with a shout and with the voice of the archangel and the trump of God.

138
00:12:24,640 --> 00:12:28,060
And John had contemplated for a little bit what that might mean.

139
00:12:28,060 --> 00:12:36,540
And he had thought of a shout, and he had thought of a trump, and he had thought of the voice of the archangel,

140
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:43,620
but he did not realize nor did he dream that it would be like this when it happened.

141
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:47,500
There was a shout, but it was more than just a shout.

142
00:12:47,580 --> 00:12:48,520
It ripped the air.

143
00:12:49,120 --> 00:12:53,040
It pierced to the very center of the earth, to the very marrow of his bones.

144
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:56,180
And John had stopped everything.

145
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:59,920
And John Jones knew that this was it.

146
00:13:00,660 --> 00:13:02,120
And he began to cry out,

147
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:05,100
Oh, no, Lord.

148
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:06,760
No, no, not yet.

149
00:13:06,820 --> 00:13:08,000
I am not ready, Lord.

150
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:11,860
And then all at once, as if by magic instantaneously,

151
00:13:12,860 --> 00:13:14,900
his heart had stopped beating.

152
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,440
And there had been a change.

153
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:19,920
His hands were cold and clammy and lifeless.

154
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:24,260
And in the wink of an eye, there had been a change come over him.

155
00:13:24,920 --> 00:13:29,140
And half a block down the street, the Coca-Cola truck had wrecked, and it turned over.

156
00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:31,760
And beverages were spilling out into the street.

157
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:33,580
And he thought, is the driver hurt?

158
00:13:33,660 --> 00:13:36,840
And then he realized, what difference does it make if the driver is killed?

159
00:13:36,940 --> 00:13:39,660
Everyone is killed, and yet everyone is still alive.

160
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:41,560
It was a state of emergency.

161
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:44,560
Everything was thrown into upheaval and chaos.

162
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:49,220
And suddenly there struck a cross of the day's mind of John Jones, one thought,

163
00:13:49,560 --> 00:13:51,160
I must get home.

164
00:13:52,060 --> 00:13:54,700
I must get home as quickly as I possibly can.

165
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:59,520
And he turned and began running down the same street that he had walked up just moments before.

166
00:13:59,900 --> 00:14:02,660
But it seemed like an eternity, a lifetime ago.

167
00:14:02,660 --> 00:14:08,340
And the white, neat, trimmed houses were rocking and reeling, and they were crumbling.

168
00:14:09,120 --> 00:14:13,340
And as John passed that section of sidewalk that was cracked, broken,

169
00:14:13,640 --> 00:14:15,440
he thought, what difference does that make now?

170
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:19,420
Because the whole street had opened up into a deep, wide-open chasm,

171
00:14:19,660 --> 00:14:29,580
and cars and trees, and the auto, the car of the Williams boy and the Ingram girl tumbling down into it.

172
00:14:29,580 --> 00:14:42,020
And John ran without hearing the sound of his steps,

173
00:14:42,620 --> 00:14:46,800
but feeling the crude vibration of his feet pounding the sidewalk.

174
00:14:47,400 --> 00:14:49,200
And he ran as hard as he could run.

175
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:55,280
And suddenly there arose across the vision of this man a spectacle that he could not believe.

176
00:14:55,280 --> 00:14:59,740
He thought that he was imagining things.

177
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:04,720
And he told himself half-consciously,

178
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:06,960
I must watch and see if this happens again.

179
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:10,120
And suddenly there from the lawn of the Johnson family,

180
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:13,920
the ground opened up, and a body came slithering through the ground

181
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:16,500
and drifting into the air.

182
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:17,420
It was a judgment.

183
00:15:18,740 --> 00:15:20,680
Bodies were coming from the ground all over,

184
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:22,720
and John ran as hard as he could run.

185
00:15:23,500 --> 00:15:26,940
Now he could see the road slatteth on the porch of his little home.

186
00:15:27,020 --> 00:15:28,160
He had to get home quickly.

187
00:15:28,860 --> 00:15:30,740
Mary, Billy, and Susan is there.

188
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:35,700
Now he was there.

189
00:15:35,780 --> 00:15:38,420
He turns up the walk and runs through the door that was open,

190
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:39,300
and he screams, Mary!

191
00:15:40,160 --> 00:15:41,760
And there is no answer.

192
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:43,380
And groping blindly,

193
00:15:43,380 --> 00:15:47,240
he fumbles down the hall to the bedroom,

194
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:49,860
and there's the bed empty, unmade.

195
00:15:50,580 --> 00:15:51,660
Mary is gone.

196
00:15:52,040 --> 00:15:53,580
And he started down the hall

197
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:58,480
and stumbled sprawling headlong across a piece of broken furniture,

198
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:01,420
and he raises and pulls himself up

199
00:16:01,420 --> 00:16:02,520
and looks into Billy's room.

200
00:16:02,580 --> 00:16:02,980
He's gone.

201
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:04,080
Susan is gone.

202
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:06,940
And he stumbled to the kitchen.

203
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:07,920
There was no Mary.

204
00:16:09,300 --> 00:16:10,260
Dishes were broken.

205
00:16:10,400 --> 00:16:12,340
The kitchen was in general disarray.

206
00:16:12,340 --> 00:16:15,640
And there on the counter was a note that he had left Mary

207
00:16:15,640 --> 00:16:17,540
telling her that he was walking to work,

208
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:19,020
that the car was in the garage,

209
00:16:19,340 --> 00:16:22,260
and that there was a coffee pot that he had left on.

210
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:24,840
But Mary was gone.

211
00:16:25,740 --> 00:16:27,900
And suddenly John Jones knew.

212
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:30,720
Mary was ready to go.

213
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:33,480
Billy and Susan were ready to go.

214
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:36,940
And then I am here all alone.

215
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:39,640
And then he thought,

216
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:41,180
Well, now, if they're gone,

217
00:16:41,180 --> 00:16:42,760
I must go too,

218
00:16:42,860 --> 00:16:44,260
because God said that,

219
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:48,000
Jesus said that all men shall be gathered before me,

220
00:16:48,260 --> 00:16:49,120
before him.

221
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:54,360
And one thought waged itself into the numb mind of John Jones.

222
00:16:54,360 --> 00:16:57,380
I must hide.

223
00:16:58,100 --> 00:16:59,120
I must hide.

224
00:16:59,240 --> 00:17:01,180
I cannot let God find me here.

225
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:02,440
And then he thought,

226
00:17:03,060 --> 00:17:04,260
Where can I hide?

227
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:05,720
And then the basement.

228
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:06,820
He thought of the basement.

229
00:17:07,140 --> 00:17:09,220
And he opened the door and thrust his body through

230
00:17:09,220 --> 00:17:11,020
and fell sprawling to the basement floor

231
00:17:11,020 --> 00:17:14,220
because the steps had broken away from the doorway.

232
00:17:14,220 --> 00:17:17,640
And he felt something that was damp with his hands.

233
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:20,080
And it was a ruptured fuel tank.

234
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:22,420
And oil was on his hands.

235
00:17:22,560 --> 00:17:25,800
And then he was horrified with the thought of fire.

236
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:27,180
What if a fire should happen?

237
00:17:27,180 --> 00:17:30,180
And then ironically and bitterly,

238
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:32,080
John Jones began to laugh.

239
00:17:32,520 --> 00:17:33,620
A fire, he thought.

240
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:36,740
Peter said that the world and all that is therein

241
00:17:36,740 --> 00:17:37,920
shall be burnt up.

242
00:17:38,240 --> 00:17:41,160
What difference will a hundred gallon of fuel oil make or not?

243
00:17:41,640 --> 00:17:43,600
And he pulled himself to his knees

244
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:45,220
and began to crawl into a corner.

245
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:48,480
He must find some place to hide

246
00:17:48,480 --> 00:17:51,760
because he is not ready to meet God.

247
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:54,140
And he put his face,

248
00:17:54,420 --> 00:17:55,820
to crawl into a dark corner.

249
00:17:56,420 --> 00:17:58,140
And he put his face into his hands

250
00:17:58,140 --> 00:17:59,280
and he began to plead.

251
00:17:59,740 --> 00:18:00,580
Please God.

252
00:18:00,940 --> 00:18:01,700
Please God.

253
00:18:02,060 --> 00:18:03,240
Please cover me up.

254
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:05,320
Please let the house fall on me.

255
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:06,860
Why was I ever born?

256
00:18:07,300 --> 00:18:08,600
Please God, let me die.

257
00:18:08,740 --> 00:18:10,300
Let me become non-existent.

258
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:14,320
But there's one thing that John Jones never asked himself.

259
00:18:14,840 --> 00:18:15,900
He never asked himself,

260
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:16,640
John Jones,

261
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:19,700
why have you waited so long to pray for God's help?

262
00:18:19,700 --> 00:18:22,860
John, why didn't you obey your Lord a long time ago?

263
00:18:23,300 --> 00:18:26,140
Why did you act and live as if your God did not exist?

264
00:18:26,720 --> 00:18:29,580
Why did you act as if the Lord had been crucified

265
00:18:29,580 --> 00:18:32,120
